# Descricoes do catalogo em ingles — o idioma padrao do app.
# Formato: nome<TAB>texto. Um por linha.
# Gerado por tool/rewrite_catalog_descriptions.dart

Qwen 3 0.6B (LiteRT-LM)	Smallest LiteRT-LM general-purpose chat model for low-RAM phones
Qwen 2.5 1.5B Instruct (LiteRT-LM)	Balanced LiteRT-LM chat model with int8 quantization
DeepSeek R1 Distill Qwen 1.5B (LiteRT-LM)	Reasoning-focused LiteRT-LM model with int8 quantization
LFM2.5 230M (Q4_0)	Smallest model here — runs on anything. The benchmark model, so it has to be one that answers: see the QAT/QAD note above
SmolLM2 135M (Q4_K_M)	The smallest thing here that still speaks, and the next candidate for the CPU benchmark — lighter than the 230M, but not the benchmark yet because the pass/fail thresholds are calibrated against the 230M on a Galaxy A72, and those need re-measuring before they describe this model
LFM2.5 350M (Q4_0)	4-bit, tuned for edge devices
LFM2.5 1.2B Instruct (Q4_0)	4-bit. Multilingual, and the sweet spot for most phones
LFM2.5 2.6B (Q4_0)	4-bit, the largest LFM2.5 that still fits comfortably
LFM2.5-VL 450M (Q4_0 + vision)	Smallest vision-language model here. 209 MB of weights plus a 98 MB projector
LFM2.5-VL 1.6B (Q4_0 + vision)	The sweet spot of the VL line. The projector is 556 MB, so vision costs more than the weights
LFM2.5-VL 3B (Q4_0 + vision)	Largest LFM2.5-VL. Same 556 MB projector as the 1.6B, so the step up buys text quality only
Spark X2.5 1.7B (Q4_K_M)	New architecture (LLM_ARCH_SPARK2_5), text only. Needs the engine from the 2026-09-23 sync
Spark X2.5 4B (Q4_K_M)	Largest Spark. Same architecture requirement as the 1.7B; needs a roomy phone
Qwen3.5 0.8B (Q4_K_M + vision)	Multimodal at 0.8B. 195 MB projector, so about 700 MB with vision
Qwen3.5 2B (Q4_K_M + vision)	The balanced Qwen3.5. 637 MB projector on top of the weights
Qwen3.5 4B (Q4_K_M + vision)	Best quality under 4B here, and multimodal. 641 MB projector; a vision turn needs ~3.2 GB
Ministral 3 3B Instruct (Q4_K_M + vision)	Mistral's own weights, ungated. Vision needs the 803 MB BF16 projector — the heaviest one here
Phi-4-mini Instruct 3.8B (Q4_K_M)	Microsoft, MIT licence. Strong at reasoning for its size, text only
SmolLM3 3B (Q4_K_M)	HuggingFace's own 3B, in the llama.cpp org's repo. Text only; reasoning variant exists upstream
SmolVLM2 2.2B Instruct (Q4_K_M + vision)	The larger sibling of the 500M already listed. 565 MB projector; good at screenshots and UI
Gemma 3 270M Instruct (QAT Q4_0)	The smallest useful text model here. For testing the pipeline, not for answers
Gemma 3 1B Instruct (QAT Q4_0)	Quantisation-aware 4-bit. Google's own QAT weights, mirrored ungated
Gemma 3 4B Instruct (QAT Q4_0)	Quantisation-aware 4-bit with vision. Needs a 0.85 GB projector
Gemma 4 E2B Instruct (QAT Q4_0)	Quantisation-aware 4-bit — text, images and audio. Needs a 0.99 GB projector
Gemma 4 E4B Instruct (QAT Q4_0)	Quantisation-aware 4-bit — text, images and audio. Needs a 0.99 GB projector and a roomy phone
Gemma 4 E2B Instruct (GGUF)	Multimodal — text, images and audio, with GPU offload. Needs a 0.52 GB projector
Qwen2.5-Omni 3B (GGUF)	Omni — images and audio in, text out. Needs a 1.43 GB projector
Qwen2.5-VL 3B Instruct (GGUF)	Vision — strong at reading text in images. Needs a 0.79 GB projector
SmolVLM2 500M Video (GGUF)	Vision — tiny and quick, for trying image input cheaply. 0.10 GB projector
Gemma 4 E2B Instruct (LiteRT-LM)	Multimodal — reads text, images and audio. Best size/quality balance
Gemma 4 E4B Instruct (LiteRT-LM)	Multimodal — text, images and audio. Highest quality; needs ~5 GB RAM
Kimi Moonlight 16B-A3B (Q3_K_S)	Moonshot AI (Kimi) — 3B active MoE, high quality
Qwen2.5-3B Instruct (Q4_K_M)	Best balance of speed and quality for mobile
Qwen2-VL-2B Instruct (Q4_K_M)	Vision-capable model, but images run on LiteRT-LM only — here it is text
Phi-3.5 Mini Instruct (Q4_K_M)	Microsoft's compact reasoning model
Gemma 2 2B Instruct (Q4_K_M)	Google's lightweight general chat model — fast and smart
Gemma-2-2B-Abliterated (Q4_K_M)	🔓 Abliterated — Permanently uncensored, very smart
SmolLM2-1.7B-Uncensored (Q4_K_M)	Ultra-compact and unrestricted assistant
Dolphin-3.0-Qwen2.5-1.5B (Q4_K_M)	Uncensored Dolphin 3.0 — Fast and unrestricted
Llama-3.2-3B Uncensored (Q4_K_M)	Uncensored Llama 3.2 3B — Smarter and unrestricted
Llama-3.2-1B Instruct (Q4_K_M)	Ultra-lightweight text model
DreamShaper 8 LCM (SD 1.5)	Extremely fast 4-step local image generation
CyberRealistic V8 FP16 (SD 1.5)	Photorealistic, uncensored local image generation — FP16 for mobile
Realistic Vision V5.1 fp16 (SD 1.5)	Highly popular photorealistic portrait and scene model
AbsoluteReality 1.8.1 pruned (SD 1.5)	Photorealistic general-purpose image generation
AnyLoRA (SD 1.5)	Highly versatile Anime / Stylized image generator
GTE Reranker ModernBERT Base (Q4_K_M)	Cross-encoder reranker, ModernBERT, Portuguese and English. Measured on an Edge 60 at 111 ms per query with a real logit spread of 2,07. The one to start with.
GTE Reranker ModernBERT Base (Q8_0)	The same reranker in Q8_0, for when the last 0,2 of the NDCG is worth 54 MB. Verified end to end on an Edge 60.
BGE Reranker Base (Q8_0)	Cross-encoder reranker, BERT architecture, English. The head and the pooler projection are both in the file, which is the check that matters.
BCE Reranker Base v1 (Q4_K_M)	Cross-encoder reranker, BERT, English and Chinese. Well formed: cls.output.weight [768] with the 768x768 pooler beside it.
Multilingual E5 Small (Q8_0)	Embeds in 100 languages including Portuguese, mean-pooled. The one to reach for on a pt_BR device — a purely English embedder makes Portuguese search quietly bad.
BGE Small EN v1.5 (F16)	Smallest usable embedder: 33M parameters, 384 dimensions, CLS pooling. Verified on an Edge 60.
BGE Small EN v1.5 (Q8_0)	The same 33M embedder in Q8_0 — half the bytes of F16 for a 384-float vector, where the quantisation is nearly free.
E5 Small v2 (Q8_0)	Small mean-pooled embedder, English, 384 dimensions. Needs "query: " and "passage: " prefixes on the two sides, as every E5 does.
Nomic Embed Text v1.5 (Q4_K_M)	Long-context embedder, 8k, mean-pooled, 768 dimensions. The only screened option that embeds a whole document in one pass.
ModernBERT Embed Base (Q8_0)	ModernBERT embedder, mean-pooled, 768 dimensions. The same architecture as the reranker above, so it is worth having both to see the difference a scoring head makes.
BGE Reranker v2 M3 (Q4_K_M)	568M, multilingual, arch bert. Carries both cls.output.weight and pooler, and that pair is what decides whether a score is a score — the jina v1 file above has the head without the pooler and returns a number in (-1,1) that ranks plausibly. Twice the size of the BGE Reranker Base and multilingual, which on a pt_BR phone is the part that matters.
BGE Reranker v2 M3 (Q2_K)	The same reranker in Q2_K: 69 MB cheaper for a quantisation that costs a little ordering rather than the shape of the answer.
Jina Reranker v2 Base Multilingual (Q4_K_M)	278M, arch bert, head and pooler both present. The smallest reranker here that returns a real logit — and it is the v2 of a family whose v1 is in this catalogue and does not work, so the version in the name is the entire difference.
Qwen3 Reranker 4B (Q4_K_M)	The strongest reranker screened, and the first qwen3 the app treats as an encoder. It declares its own pooling_type=rank and carries cls.output.weight [2560, 2] with yes/no labels — the head llama.cpp loads for LLM_ARCH_QWEN3. Unmeasured: every number this catalogue quotes is the ModernBERT above, and a qwen3 has never run here.
Qwen3 Reranker 4B (Q2_K)	The same 4B reranker in Q2_K: 2,4 GB becomes 1,7 GB. The size is what decides this one, and 4B is already the top of the range this app is aimed at.
Qwen3 Embedding 0.6B (Q8_0)	Published by Qwen itself. Arch qwen3, declares pooling_type=last, 1024 dimensions. The only embedder here that is a decoder rather than a BERT, and the one that reads a whole document in a single pass — which is the actual argument for it over the 80 MB Nomic above.
